    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on high-upside matchups today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (77.56) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.10). **Gunnar Henderson** remains our strongest play; despite facing an elite hold pitcher in Melton, the combination of his premium batting order spot and an advantageous park factor provides a robust floor for both power and our league-leading pursuit of stolen bases. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against Lorenzen, where a 19% boost from the starter\u2019s skill profile and a favorable platoon advantage solidify his status as an anchor for the outfield. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) also warrants attention, as he faces a vulnerable Bieber, with a dynamic platoon edge and a prime #2 spot in the order driving his elite rating.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s slate involved the benching of **Coby Mayo** (45.28). While he shows solid raw power, his projected efficiency fell just short of our starters due to a negative platoon split against Melton and a lower-leverage spot in the lineup. He ultimately yielded to the superior platoon utility of **Nasim Nunez** (66.19) and the specific speed requirements of our roster. We are exercising caution with **Sam Antonacci** (47.88), who faces the toughest assignment of the day against Cole. While his position at the top of the lineup provides a slight boost, he is a marginal start who is only active due to the necessity of maintaining lineup coverage. Managers should monitor **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (55.35) closely; despite his high talent ceiling, a difficult matchup against Cavalli has suppressed his expected efficiency, making him a high-variance play that requires careful monitoring of his initial at-bats.",
